{"data":{"attachmentkeynames":["rs"],"desc":"Appends a human NOTE to one kb.plan entry (found by exact claim): pushes {text, author, time} onto the entry's `notes` array and writes the facet through the journaled dev.code.patch_control_facet (label 'plan note: ...'). Author is resolved from the calling session (fallback plan-board). Because a note is an append it commutes with any other write, so there is no base param: it re-reads and re-applies on stale_base (up to 4 tries), each write still base-hashed against its own read - nothing forced, nothing lost. The agent side: agent.plan.step_item feeds every note into the NEXT step prompt, flags the ones it has not yet seen (no `seen_at`) as NEW, and stamps seen_at on them in its post-turn write; the plan worker's park fingerprint includes the note count, so a note also un-parks a blocked/parked item. Max 8000 chars. Returns FLAT {status, notes (count), time, author, lifecycle, hash}.","import":"use ndata::dataarray::DataArray;","params":[{"name":"claim","type":"String"},{"name":"note","type":"String"},{"name":"nn_sessionid","type":"String"}],"returntype":"FLAT","type":"rust"},"id":"sgxusm1a1689003c3wf4","readers":[],"time":1792755658904,"username":"system","writers":[]}